cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "LEO-NTN Predictive Handover: a reproducible research framework for ephemeris-aided satellite handover in 5G non-terrestrial networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Weikun
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-15"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - LEO
  - non-terrestrial networks
  - 5G NTN
  - handover
  - mobility management
  - simulation
abstract: >-
  Python framework that simulates satellite-level handover for a single user in a LEO constellation
  (SGP4-propagated Walker-delta or TLE/OMM constellations, 3GPP TR 38.821 Set-1 S-band link budget,
  simplified TR 38.811 LOS/NLOS blockage and shadowing) and compares greedy, A3-style and
  ephemeris-based handover rules with an ephemeris-aided, measurement-corrected, cost-aware predictive
  rule under ephemeris timing errors, measurement noise, blockage and handover execution delay.
